            {
              "id": "cf9a162",
              "elType": "widget",
              "settings": {
                "editor": "<p>Peace is stronger when more voices are brought into the light. Women remain underrepresented in decisions on peace, security and conflict prevention, despite experiencing their consequences in distinct ways.</p>",
                "text_color": "#2A3B32",
                "typography_typography": "custom",
                "typography_font_family": "Manrope",
                "typography_font_size": {
                  "unit": "px",
                  "size": 17,
                  "sizes": []
                },
                "typography_line_height": {
                  "unit": "em",
                  "size": 1.72,
                  "sizes": []
                },
                "align": "left"
              },
              "elements": [],
              "widgetType": "text-editor"
            },
            {
              "id": "193d3d9",
              "elType": "widget",
              "settings": {
                "space": {
                  "unit": "px",
                  "size": 18,
                  "sizes": []
                }
              },
              "elements": [],
              "widgetType": "spacer"
            },
            {
              "id": "7239a3a",
              "elType": "widget",
              "settings": {
                "editor": "<p>The conference brings women\u2019s perspectives closer to the centre of regional dialogue, while supporting the wider Women, Peace and Security agenda \u2014 including Malaysia\u2019s National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security 2025\u20132030, which strengthens women\u2019s participation and leadership across peacebuilding, prevention and national security.</p>",
                "text_color": "#2A3B32",
                "typography_typography": "custom",
                "typography_font_family": "Manrope",
                "typography_font_size": {
                  "unit": "px",
